<?xml version='1.0' encoding='utf-8'?>
<graphml xmlns="http://graphml.graphdrawing.org/xmlns" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:schemaLocation="http://graphml.graphdrawing.org/xmlns http://graphml.graphdrawing.org/xmlns/1.0/graphml.xsd">
  <key id="d11" for="edge" attr.name="type" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d10" for="edge" attr.name="seq" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d9" for="edge" attr.name="notes" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d8" for="edge" attr.name="flow_id" attr.type="long" />
  <key id="d7" for="node" attr.name="notes" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d6" for="node" attr.name="service" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d5" for="node" attr.name="name" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d4" for="graph" attr.name="graph_usable" attr.type="boolean" />
  <key id="d3" for="graph" attr.name="categories" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d2" for="graph" attr.name="notes" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d1" for="graph" attr.name="link" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d0" for="graph" attr.name="name" attr.type="string" />
  <graph edgedefault="directed">
    <node id="0">
      <data key="d5">Developer</data>
      <data key="d6">UserCompanyDeveloper</data>
      <data key="d7">Commits application code, build definitions and CloudFormation templates to the repository. Can change the build or the infrastructure on demand by modifying the repository (going back to the first stage).</data>
    </node>
    <node id="1">
      <data key="d5">CodePipeline</data>
      <data key="d6">CodePipeline</data>
      <data key="d7">Orchestrates the stages: source (CodeCommit), build (CodeBuild), deploy (CloudFormation). Moves each commit to the next stage automatically. Parallel deploy stages accommodate up to 100 customers.</data>
    </node>
    <node id="2">
      <data key="d5">CodeCommit</data>
      <data key="d6">CodeCommit</data>
      <data key="d7">AWS source repository. Holds the application code and the CloudFormation templates that define the entire application infrastructure.</data>
    </node>
    <node id="3">
      <data key="d5">CodeBuild</data>
      <data key="d6">CodeBuild</data>
      <data key="d7">Build stage. Spins up a container and is paid for only for the duration of the build. The build is controlled by the developer through the repository. On a successful build it outputs a container image to ECR.</data>
    </node>
    <node id="4">
      <data key="d5">CloudFormation</data>
      <data key="d6">CloudFormation</data>
      <data key="d7">Deploy stage, chosen over CodeDeploy, the ECS task definition deployer and Lambda because it also deploys the underlying infrastructure. One baseline template is used for all production environments, with a small per-customer configuration (VPC name, ECS cluster). Runs in parallel to up to 100 customer VPCs. Three-step process: 1) change set, 2) approve or reject by someone with the proper roles and permissions, 3) execute the change set.</data>
    </node>
    <node id="5">
      <data key="d5">ECR Registry</data>
      <data key="d6">ECR</data>
      <data key="d7">Container registry that stores the built application image, ready to be deployed.</data>
    </node>
    <node id="6">
      <data key="d5">VPC</data>
      <data key="d6">VPC</data>
      <data key="d7">Production environment. Each customer is deployed to a different VPC (up to 100), all receiving the same changes from the single template. Developer environments are kept separate from production and client QA environments.</data>
    </node>
    <node id="7">
      <data key="d5">ECS</data>
      <data key="d6">ECS</data>
      <data key="d7">Elastic Container Service task definition deployed by CloudFormation to run the application image. The cluster name comes from the per-customer configuration.</data>
    </node>
    <node id="8">
      <data key="d5">IAM</data>
      <data key="d6">IAM</data>
      <data key="d7">IAM roles and permissions required by the application, deployed by CloudFormation.</data>
    </node>
    <node id="9">
      <data key="d5">ALB</data>
      <data key="d6">ALB</data>
      <data key="d7">Application load balancer required by the application, deployed by CloudFormation.</data>
    </node>
    <edge source="0" target="2" id="0">
      <data key="d8">0</data>
      <data key="d9">Developer commits code changes to the CodeCommit repository.</data>
      <data key="d10">0</data>
      <data key="d11">data</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="2" target="3" id="0">
      <data key="d8">0</data>
      <data key="d9">The pipeline moves the commit into the next stage, CodeBuild.</data>
      <data key="d10">1</data>
      <data key="d11">data</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="2" target="0" id="0">
      <data key="d8">2</data>
      <data key="d9">Drawn arrow; the developer can go back to the first stage at any time to modify the build or infrastructure through the repository.</data>
      <data key="d10">0</data>
      <data key="d11">meta</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="3" target="5" id="0">
      <data key="d8">0</data>
      <data key="d9">At the end of a successful build, CodeBuild outputs the application container image to the ECR registry.</data>
      <data key="d10">2</data>
      <data key="d11">data</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="3" target="2" id="0">
      <data key="d8">2</data>
      <data key="d9">Drawn arrow; the build is controlled by what the developer defines in the repository.</data>
      <data key="d10">1</data>
      <data key="d11">meta</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="4" target="5" id="0">
      <data key="d8">1</data>
      <data key="d9">Drawn arrow, not described in the audio; presumably the deployment referencing the application image in the registry.</data>
      <data key="d10">1</data>
      <data key="d11">data</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="4" target="6" id="0">
      <data key="d8">1</data>
      <data key="d9">CloudFormation deploys the infrastructure and application to the customer VPC by change set, approval, then execute. Pushes the same changes in parallel to up to 100 VPCs.</data>
      <data key="d10">2</data>
      <data key="d11">control</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="4" target="7" id="0">
      <data key="d8">1</data>
      <data key="d9">CloudFormation deploys the ECS task definition.</data>
      <data key="d10">2'</data>
      <data key="d11">control</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="4" target="8" id="0">
      <data key="d8">1</data>
      <data key="d9">CloudFormation deploys the IAM role and permissions.</data>
      <data key="d10">2''</data>
      <data key="d11">control</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="4" target="9" id="0">
      <data key="d8">1</data>
      <data key="d9">CloudFormation deploys the application load balancer.</data>
      <data key="d10">2'''</data>
      <data key="d11">control</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="5" target="4" id="0">
      <data key="d8">1</data>
      <data key="d9">As soon as the build is done and the image is in the registry, the CloudFormation deploy stage is kicked off.</data>
      <data key="d10">0</data>
      <data key="d11">control</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="5" target="3" id="0">
      <data key="d8">2</data>
      <data key="d9">Drawn arrow, not described in the audio; presumably feedback from the registry to the build stage.</data>
      <data key="d10">2</data>
      <data key="d11">meta</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="6" target="4" id="0">
      <data key="d8">1</data>
      <data key="d9">Drawn arrow, not described in the audio; presumably deployment status or feedback from the VPC to CloudFormation.</data>
      <data key="d10">3</data>
      <data key="d11">meta</data>
    </edge>
    <data key="d0">Aetion: Streamlined Application and Infrastructure Deployment with CodePipeline and CloudFormation</data>
    <data key="d1">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=6YkguepAQuQ</data>
    <data key="d2">Healthcare analytics company streamlines the path from developer commit to production. A pipeline runs CodeCommit (source), then CodeBuild (build container image, push to ECR), then CloudFormation (deploy stage). CloudFormation deploys the application and its infrastructure (ECS task definition, IAM role, ALB) into per-customer VPCs, with parallel stages for up to 100 customers from a single template. Governance is a three-step deploy: change set, approval, execute.</data>
    <data key="d3">DevOps, CI/CD, Containers, Infrastructure as Code, Healthcare Analytics</data>
    <data key="d4">True</data>
  </graph>
</graphml>
